    correctAnswer: "Psychological Assessment",
    notes: `<b>PSYCHOLOGICAL ASSESSMENT</b><br><br><b>1. Definition</b><br><br>Psychological Assessment is the process of gathering and evaluating information about a person's behavior, abilities, personality, and mental functioning to understand the person and make informed decisions.<br><br><b>2. Explanation</b><br><br>Psychological assessment helps psychologists understand a person's strengths, weaknesses, and possible difficulties.<br><br>It involves gathering information from different sources, such as psychological tests, interviews, observations, and personal history.<br><br>The psychologist examines the information as a whole rather than relying on just one test score.<br><br><b>Key idea:</b> Psychological assessment involves gathering and interpreting information to understand a person.<br><br><b>3. Example</b><br><br>A psychologist assesses a student who is having difficulty in school.<br><br>The psychologist:<br><ul><li>Gives an intelligence test to assess cognitive abilities.</li><li>Interviews the student to understand their experiences.</li><li>Observes the student's behavior.</li><li>Reviews relevant school records.</li></ul>The psychologist combines the information to understand the student's difficulties and determine what support may be helpful.<br><br><b>4. What to Remember for CFE</b><br><ul><li>Assessment involves gathering and interpreting information.</li><li>It may use tests, interviews, observations, and records.</li><li>It examines a person's abilities, behavior, personality, or mental functioning.</li><li>It supports decisions, such as identifying learning needs or planning treatment.</li><li>Assessment is broader than simply giving a psychological test.</li></ul><b>Important distinction:</b><br><ul><li><b>Psychological Testing:</b> Uses tests to measure specific characteristics or abilities.</li><li><b>Psychological Assessment:</b> Combines and interprets information from different sources to understand a person.</li></ul><b>5. Situational Application</b><br><br><b>Situation:</b> A psychologist gives a student an intelligence test, conducts an interview, observes the student's behavior, and reviews school records before recommending appropriate learning support.<br><br><b>Question:</b> What process is the psychologist conducting?<br><br><b>Answer:</b> Psychological Assessment.<br><br><b>Explanation:</b> The psychologist gathers information from multiple sources and interprets the findings to understand the student's needs.<br><br><b>6. CFE Tip: How to Recognize It</b><br><br>Look for these clues:<br><ul><li>Gathering information from multiple sources.</li><li>Combining test results, interviews, and observations.</li><li>Understanding a person's strengths and weaknesses.</li><li>Making recommendations based on the overall findings.</li></ul><b>Quick memory trick:</b><br><br><b>Psychological Assessment = Gather + Interpret + Understand.</b>`
